#	Architecture Decision Records

ADR 01: Cold Data Tiering to AWS S3: 
	  Context: Analysis shows ~48% (~612 TiB) of physical NAS data has not been accessed in over two years. Finance declined a full flash refresh (~1.3 PiB). Cold data includes archives, legal hold, and low activity datasets.
    Problem: Keeping all data on flash is cost prohibitive and wastes high performance storage on inactive datasets.
Decision:
•	Tier cold data to AWS S3 Standard IA for retrievable datasets.
•	Use S3 Glacier Deep Archive for legal hold and long term retention.
•	Maintain EU residency by storing EU cold data in EU West region buckets.
Alternatives considered:
•	Keep all data on flash (too costly).
•	FabricPool tiering only (limited to snapshot only in current estate).
•	Deletion (ownership gaps, compliance risk).
Consequences:
•	Reduces flash requirement (~700 TiB vs 1.3 PiB).
•	Retrieval latency for Glacier data must be managed.
•	Requires metadata tracking for rollback and audit.
•	Ensures compliance with residency and GxP constraints.
